  "ref": "EZK.35.8",
  "review_notes": [
    "The three *in*s are given to the present בְּ under rule 25's distributed-scope clause. The defensible alternative is rule 33: read the fronted nouns as adverbial accusatives, give each its own supplied *in*, and mark בְּ unrepresented with the suffix. I took the first because a present morpheme takes its English before a supplied reading does.",
    "*with its slain* is placed on the verb under rule 44's final clause (bare second accusative reached through a supplied preposition); the competing reading treats חֲלָלָיו as an accusative of material and gives *with* to the noun under rule 33."
  ]
